{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch1S99jpAwbrojG2u7sqi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DYjdarcXPntQzY8MKfUMpQ","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"report":"SCOPE OF THIS PAYLOAD (32/32)\nFiles changed in this payload:\n- .claude/scripts/subprocess-test-baseline.json (new)\n- tier_policy_cli/{_types,learn,loader}.py\n- validate-governance.sh\n- .claude/settings.json\n- the PR template\n- validate-pair-rail-verdict.py\n- coverage.yml, validate.yml\n- CHANGELOG [1.4.4]\n- INSTALL.md, Makefile\n- README/README.pt-BR, SBOM/SECURITY/VERSIONING\n- SPEC audit-log row\n- VERSION, npm/package.json, pyproject.toml\n- docs/* counts and restore lines\n- scripts/_codex_harness.sh\n- scripts/install-npm.sh\n\nI read each one against the candidate tree. scripts/upgrade.sh is withheld from the copy, so the condition-12 exit-2 message was seen only in an older staged copy (.claude/plans/PLAN-180/staged-s313/scripts/upgrade.sh:607-610).\n\nDECLARED CONDITIONS CHECKED AGAINST CODE (all hold where this payload gives evidence)\n- C5: _KERNEL_PATHS has 123 entries (check_arbitration_kernel.py:91-347). The 13 new rows are at :309-315, :332-336 and :340. coverage.yml timeout-minutes goes from 35 to 50.\n- C8: _python-hook.sh:410 exports CEO_HOOK_BOUNDED_EXIT=1.\n- C9 / C10:\n  - The pin manifest has package_version 0.160.0 (codex-cli-pin-manifest.json:3), and CODEX_VERSION_FLOOR is \"0.160.0\" (cli_currency.py:11).\n  - The oracle's route is compatible/version_floor_only (_pair_rail_parts/part_01.py:566-568).\n  - validate-pair-rail-verdict.py:768-784 skips the payload-hash compare for a declared codex_cli that is newer than the manifest and at or above the floor, as declared.\n  - model_currency.py:7-16 admits the families and refuses only claude-opus-4-1, as declared.\n  - validate-governance.sh:717-727 and tier_policy_cli loader.py:251 / learn.py:462 call it.\n- C11: the CHANGELOG \"Version number.\" paragraph matches.\n- C12: _release_bump_sites.py:90 rewrites exactly the three upgrade lines in INSTALL.md (:717, :719, :722). The \"-rc.1\" suffix is kept.\n- C3 spot-check: sys.dont_write_bytecode is set early in audit_spool_state.py:62 and check-audit-real-loss.py:67. malformed_record_id_files is present.\n- SPEC row vs code: _audit_emit_parts/lifecycle_schemas.py:508/516 carry bash_indirect and the two switch names.\n- Counts: 78 top-level _lib modules, 341 recursive, 201 ADR files, all confirmed in the copy.\n\nItems 1-6 of WHAT TO VERIFY:\n1. Adopter blast radius: no hook changes in this payload.\n   - Agent model: values in the old literal list still pass (validate-governance.sh:718). Others now go through model_currency; before, every one of them was an error, so nothing that passed before is refused now.\n   - The settings.json changes (cleanupPeriodDays 3650, claudeMdExcludes) are dogfood only. Installs build from templates/settings/settings.base.json, which still has 90 (:671).\n   - claude_md_excludes.root_claude_md_excluded only matches the new pattern when the checkout itself sits under .claude/plans/**/staged*/.\n2. Fail direction:\n   - parse_pin_range now raises on a malformed body, which gives INVALID (closed; before, the line was skipped).\n   - If the module-level `_lib` import fails, the exit code is 1. release.yml:719 runs under set -euo pipefail, so the release blocks (a release gate, not a hook).\n   - A missing python3 or model_currency.py in validate-governance only affects ids that were already errors.\n3. Writes: nothing new in this payload writes outside its place.\n4. Moved code: tier_policy_cli/_types.py puts .claude/hooks at sys.path[0].\n   - No top-level hook module collides with the fallback imports (apply/learn/loader/_types/_constants/cli).\n   - _lib/__init__.py has no side effects.\n   - If the import fails, it falls back to strict membership.\n5. Honesty: see the P2 items.\n6. Python 3.9 / stdlib-only: all changed Python is stdlib-only with no syntax newer than 3.9.\n\nFINDINGS (P0 / P1): none in this payload.\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex): none. No undeclared P1 was found in this payload.\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\nP2-1 .github/scripts/validate-pair-rail-verdict.py:772 (message at :783)\n- Problem: exact_payload_pin is False whenever version_comparison != 0 and the CLI is at or above the floor. It does not require the CLI to be newer than the manifest version.\n- Scenario: after a future re-pin to package_version 0.170.0, a verdict declaring codex_cli 0.165.0 (older than the manifest but above the floor) skips the payload-sha compare, and :783 says it is \"newer than the payload manifest version\". The oracle (cli_currency.compatible_package_version :49) requires manifest_comparison > 0, so the two disagree.\n- Not reachable today, because manifest 0.160.0 equals the floor. It adds little beyond the declared Known-open \"validator does not bind a declared version to its payload hash\".\n- Fix: exact_payload_pin = not (version_comparison is not None and version_comparison > 0 and newer_floor is not None and newer_floor >= 0).\n\nP2-2 .claude/scripts/tier_policy_cli/learn.py:462 and loader.py:251, against apply.py:401 and cli.py:332-361\n- Problem: learn and loader now admit family ids that apply/owner-sign refuse, and _tier_rank (learn.py:535-564) ranks them -1.\n- Effects:\n  - A move away from an unranked family current tier (allowed by the loader now) is signed \"promote\" with signature_required=False. This is the PLAN-169 W2.10 F2 inversion class.\n  - A family-id winner is always signed \"demote\".\n  - Sparse family records (bare claude-haiku-4-5, gpt-5) now enter cells and lower n_min.\n- Today no write happens: an unpriced tier makes the cost-delta check return None (apply.py:266-269), so the move is cost_gated; :401 and owner-sign refuse unranked ids. But the recommendation and audit stream mislabel the direction.\n- The CHANGELOG names only the loader, not the learner.\n- Fix: keep learn.py on strict VALID_MODEL_IDS membership, or make _direction refuse/hold when either rank < 0. Mention the learner in Known-open.\n\nP2-3 INSTALL.md:717\n- Problem: if no v1.4.4-rc.* tag is present (fork without tags, offline pull, or the window between the bump commit and the tag push), the command substitution yields --pin \"\".\n- Scenario: in the readable staged upgrade.sh, an empty PIN_REF means no pin, and the upgrade runs from the checkout's current HEAD. The candidate upgrade.sh is withheld, so I could not confirm this.\n- Fix: make it `tag=$(git tag --list ... | head -n 1) && [ -n \"$tag\" ] && bash scripts/upgrade.sh ... --pin \"$tag\"`, or have upgrade.sh refuse an explicit empty --pin.\n\nP2-4 scripts/_codex_harness.sh:46, :294, :372-373, :461 (declared in the CHANGELOG, follow-up only)\n- Problem: CODEX_VERIFIED_VERSION=0.160.0 now makes three false or misleading statements:\n  - the arming check says \"fixtures/enforcement were certified on 0.160.0\";\n  - the requirements.toml written into the adopter repo says \"Verified against codex-cli 0.160.0\", while the fixtures date from 0.139.0;\n  - the :46 comment calls it the \"default semantic floor\", but the variable is never used as a floor (:58 hard-codes \">=0.160.0\").\n- Fix: keep the certification text on 0.139.0 in a separate constant, and use a distinct floor constant.\n\nP2-5 Stale comments that contradict the code:\n- validate-governance.sh:701-710 still says ERROR when the model is not in the working set, under the independent-mirror doctrine.\n- tier_policy_cli/_types.py:8, :143 and __init__.py:17 still say \"MODEL_ID Literal\".\n- cli.py:350 says \"claude-fable-5 is its first entry\", but the reorder put claude-opus-4-8 first.\n- release.yml:693-695: step 15 still promises payload sha equals the manifest.\n- codex-cli-pin.txt:196-198 says \"codex-cli-pin-manifest.json remains that gate\".\n- SPEC/v1/audit-log.schema.md row still says \"all four learning-loop rails\", but the enum now has five.\n- Fix: update the text.\n\nP2-6 CHANGELOG.md:348 (also :735)\n- Problem: the heading says \"no installed file changes\", but it lists the _subprocess_census.py fix. That file is a top-level .claude/scripts/*.py and is installed (install.sh:1606-1611; the CHANGELOG lists it among the six new helpers).\n- Related: check-subprocess-tests.py ships, but its default subprocess-test-baseline.json does not (only *.sh/*.py/*.yaml are copied). In an install it exits 2 with FileNotFoundError.\n- Fix: reword the heading and exclude the census pair from installs, or ship the baseline.\n\nP2-7 .claude/scripts/tier_policy_cli/_types.py:24-26\n- Problem: importing _types mutates sys.path globally (hooks dir at index 0) for every importer, including set-quality-profile.sh via _constants if it imports _types. No collision exists today, but it is a latent shadowing hazard.\n- Fix: import model_currency by file path with importlib, or append to sys.path instead of inserting at index 0.\n\nP2-8 scripts/install-npm.sh:158-163\n- Problem: the `o, = d` unpacking raises a bare traceback (fail-closed, but unclear) on a list or dict of any length other than 1.\n- Fix: check the length and print an explicit ::error.","decision":"GO-WITH-CONDITIONS","sentence":"In payload 32/32, every declared condition I could test against the code holds and I found no P0 and no undeclared P1. The weaker governance checks this payload carries (model-family allowlist, Codex version-floor route, the installer's 0.160.0 claim) are declared in the conditions and the CHANGELOG, and what remains is P2 follow-up work."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1026,"cache_read_input_tokens":233446,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1026},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagn