ests.py ships, but its default subprocess-test-baseline.json does not (only *.sh/*.py/*.yaml are copied). In an install it exits 2 with FileNotFoundError.\\n- Fix: reword the heading and exclude the census pair from installs, or ship the baseline.\\n\\nP2-7 .claude/scripts/tier_policy_cli/_types.py:24-26\\n- Problem: importing _types mutates sys.path globally (hooks dir at index 0) for every importer, including set-quality-profile.sh via _constants if it imports _types. No collision exists today, but it is a latent shadowing hazard.\\n- Fix: import model_currency by file path with importlib, or append to sys.path instead of inserting at index 0.\\n\\nP2-8 scripts/install-npm.sh:158-163\\n- Problem: the `o, = d` unpacking raises a bare traceback (fail-closed, but unclear) on a list or dict of any length other than 1.\\n- Fix: check the length and print an explicit ::error.\",\"decision\":\"GO-WITH-CONDITIONS\",\"sentence\":\"In payload 32/32, every declared condition I could test against the code holds and I found no P0 and no undeclared P1. The weaker governance checks this payload carries (model-family allowlist, Codex version-floor route, the installer's 0.160.0 claim) are declared in the conditions and the CHANGELOG, and what remains is P2 follow-up work.\"}","structured_output":{"report":"SCOPE OF THIS PAYLOAD (32/32)\nFiles changed in this payload:\n- .claude/scripts/subprocess-test-baseline.json (new)\n- tier_policy_cli/{_types,learn,loader}.py\n- validate-governance.sh\n- .claude/settings.json\n- the PR template\n- validate-pair-rail-verdict.py\n- coverage.yml, validate.yml\n- CHANGELOG [1.4.4]\n- INSTALL.md, Makefile\n- README/README.pt-BR, SBOM/SECURITY/VERSIONING\n- SPEC audit-log row\n- VERSION, npm/package.json, pyproject.toml\n- docs/* counts and restore lines\n- scripts/_codex_harness.sh\n- scripts/install-npm.sh\n\nI read each one against the candidate tree. scripts/upgrade.sh is withheld from the copy, so the condition-12 exit-2 message was seen only