ild from templates/settings/settings.base.json, which still has 90 (:671).\n   - claude_md_excludes.root_claude_md_excluded only matches the new pattern when the checkout itself sits under .claude/plans/**/staged*/.\n2. Fail direction:\n   - parse_pin_range now raises on a malformed body, which gives INVALID (closed; before, the line was skipped).\n   - If the module-level `_lib` import fails, the exit code is 1. release.yml:719 runs under set -euo pipefail, so the release blocks (a release gate, not a hook).\n   - A missing python3 or model_currency.py in validate-governance only affects ids that were already errors.\n3. Writes: nothing new in this payload writes outside its place.\n4. Moved code: tier_policy_cli/_types.py puts .claude/hooks at sys.path[0].\n   - No top-level hook module collides with the fallback imports (apply/learn/loader/_types/_constants/cli).\n   - _lib/__init__.py has no side effects.\n   - If the import fails, it falls back to strict membership.\n5. Honesty: see the P2 items.\n6. Python 3.9 / stdlib-only: all changed Python is stdlib-only with no syntax newer than 3.9.\n\nFINDINGS (P0 / P1): none in this payload.\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex): none. No undeclared P1 was found in this payload.\n\nP2 FOLLOW-UPS\nP2-1 .github/scripts/validate-pair-rail-verdict.py:772 (message at :783)\n- Problem: exact_payload_pin is False whenever version_comparison != 0 and the CLI is at or above the floor. It does not require the CLI to be newer than the manifest version.\n- Scenario: after a future re-pin to package_version 0.170.0, a verdict declaring codex_cli 0.165.0 (older than the manifest but above the floor) skips the payload-sha compare, and :783 says it is \"newer than the payload manifest version\". The oracle (cli_currency.compatible_package_version :49) requires manifest_comparison > 0, so the two disagree.\n- Not reachable today, because manifest 0.160.0 equals the floor. It adds little beyond the declared Known-open \"validator does not bind a declared version to its payload hash\".\n- Fix: exact_payload_pin = not (version_comparison is not None and version_comparison > 0 and newer_floor is not None and newer_floor >= 0).\n\nP2-2 .claude/scripts/tier_policy_cli/learn.py:462 and loader.py:251, against apply.py:401 and cli.py:332-361\n- Problem: learn and loader now admit family ids that apply/owner-sign refuse, and _tier_rank (learn.py:535-564) ranks them -1.\n- Effects:\n  - A move away from an unranked family current tier (allowed by the loader now) is signed \"promote\" with signature_required=False. This is the PLAN-169 W2.10 F2 inversion class.\n  - A family-id winner is always signed \"demote\".\n  - Sparse family records (bare claude-haiku-4-5, gpt-5) now enter cells and lower n_min.\n- Today no write happens: an unpriced tier makes the cost-delta check return None (apply.py:266-269), so the move is cost_gated; :401 and owner-sign refuse unranked ids. But the recommendation and audit stream mislabel the direction.\n- The CHANGELOG names only the loader, not the learner.\n- Fix: keep learn.py on strict VALID_MODEL_IDS membership, or make _direction refuse/hold when either rank < 0. Mention the learner in Known-open.\n\nP2-3 INSTALL.md:717\n- Problem: if no v1.4.4-rc.* tag is present (fork without tags, offline pull, or the window between the bump commit and the tag push), the command substitution yields --pin \"\".\n- Scenario: in the readable staged upgrade.sh, an empty PIN_REF means no pin, and the upgrade runs from the checkout's current HEAD. The candidate upgrade.sh is withheld, so I could not confirm this.\n- Fix: make it `tag=$(git tag --list ... | head -n 1) && [ -n \"$tag\" ] && bash scripts/upgrade.sh ... --pin \"$tag\"`, or have upgrade.sh refuse an explicit empty --pin.\n\nP2-4 scripts/_codex_harness.sh:46, :294, :372-373, :461 (declared in the CHANGELOG, follow-up only)\n- Problem: CODEX_VERIFIED_VERSION=0.160.0 now makes three false or misleading statements:\n  - the arming check says \"fix